Now you're past my analysis level; are systems in which Cauchy sequences
don't converge to a limit necessarily not Archimedean?

Regardless, in the sentence "{x_k} is a Cauchy sequence representing a real
number x", how many predicates would you use? It's sounding like you would
use two.


